      'itinerary' => json_encode([
        'Day 1 - Sacred Sites & Mountain Buddha' => 'Arrive at Gyeongju KTX Station (high-speed train from Seoul/Busan) at 1:00 PM where guide meets you. Transfer to traditional hanok accommodation in the city center (20 minutes). Check-in to beautifully preserved Korean traditional house with ondol (underfloor heating). Lunch at local restaurant featuring Gyeongju specialties: ssambap (rice with leafy wraps) and hwangnam bread (red bean pastry). Begin spiritual journey at Bulguksa Temple (2:00 PM), a UNESCO World Heritage masterpiece and one of Korea\'s most important Buddhist temples built in 751 AD. Admire elaborate wooden architecture, stone bridges (Cheongungyo and Baekungyo representing journey from earth to enlightenment), Dabotap and Seokgatap stone pagodas (depicted on 10 won coin), and beautifully landscaped gardens. Continue uphill to Seokguram Grotto (3:30 PM), an artificial stone temple on mountain slopes housing a magnificent 3.5-meter granite Buddha statue facing the East Sea - considered a masterpiece of Buddhist art and science. Experience the serene spiritual atmosphere. Return to Gyeongju city for welcome dinner at traditional Korean restaurant. Evening walk around downtown area. Rest at hanok accommodation.',
        
        'Day 2 - Royal Legacy & Celestial Wonder' => 'Morning visit (9:00 AM) to Daereungwon Tomb Complex (Tumuli Park), an extraordinary archaeological park containing 23 large ancient Silla royal burial mounds covered in grass, resembling green hills. Enter Cheonmachong (Heavenly Horse Tomb) - the only tomb open to public - to see replicated treasures and understand Silla burial customs. Walk among the massive tombs in peaceful park atmosphere - surreal and photogenic. Continue to Cheomseongdae Observatory, Asia\'s oldest existing astronomical observatory built in 632 AD, a 9-meter stone tower that helped Silla astronomers track stars. Learn about ancient Korean scientific achievements. Visit nearby Gyerim Forest, mythical birthplace of Kim clan. Lunch at Gyeongju Hanjeongsik restaurant (traditional full-course Korean meal with 12+ side dishes). Afternoon visit to Gyeongju National Museum to see invaluable Silla artifacts including the Divine Bell of King Seongdeok (largest bell in Korea), gold crowns, pottery, and Buddhist art. Free time for shopping at traditional craft stores. Evening at Donggung Palace and Wolji Pond (formerly Anapji Pond), a stunning palace complex built in 674 AD. As darkness falls, palace buildings and surrounding trees reflect perfectly in the pond\'s still water creating magical mirror images - one of Korea\'s most photographed scenes. Dinner on own with guide recommendations.',
        
        'Day 3 - Living History & Mountain Serenity' => 'Depart (8:30 AM) for Yangdong Folk Village, a UNESCO World Heritage site and Korea\'s largest traditional village preserving 500+ years of Joseon Dynasty clan culture. Walk through authentic hanok houses still inhabited by descendants of the Yangban (aristocratic) families. See thatched-roof commoner houses, tile-roof noble residences, Confucian academies, and beautiful natural setting surrounded by mountains. Understand traditional Korean class structure and lifestyle. Meet village elders and learn about Korean ancestral rituals. Participate in traditional tea ceremony at village tea house - taste Korean green tea and traditional rice cakes while learning tea etiquette. Lunch at village restaurant featuring farm-to-table Korean cuisine. Afternoon drive through scenic countryside to Girimsa Temple (founded 643 AD), a peaceful mountain temple off the typical tourist path. Experience authentic temple atmosphere away from crowds. Walk forest trails, see ancient stone pagodas, and feel the spiritual tranquility of mountain Buddhism. Visit temple museum with ancient artifacts. Return to Gyeongju for farewell dinner featuring Gyeongju Gyodong Ssambap (special rice wrapped in various leaves with 30+ side dishes) - declared UNESCO Intangible Cultural Heritage.',
        
        'Day 4 - Cultural Treasures & Farewell' => 'Final morning free time for personal exploration based on interests. Options: Visit Oreung (Five Royal Tombs) for peaceful morning walk, explore Gyeongju Historic Areas on bicycle (rental available), shop for Gyeongju crafts (traditional pottery, Silla jewelry replicas, hwangnam bread as gifts), relax at traditional Korean spa, or revisit favorite sites for better photos. Late check-out at 12:00 PM from hanok. Quick visit to Gyeongju Gyochon Traditional Village near downtown - small hanok village with Choi clan house, traditional craft workshops, and photo opportunities. Lunch at local restaurant. Transfer to Gyeongju Station for 4:00 PM departure via KTX train. Return home with deep appreciation for Korean history and unforgettable memories of ancient Silla Kingdom!',
      ]),
      'arrival' => 'Pick-up at Gyeongju Station (KTX high-speed train terminal) at 1:00 PM on Day 1. Guide will wait at main exit with "ACP Tours - Gyeongju" sign. Please book KTX train from Seoul Station (2 hours) or Busan Station (30 minutes) arriving at 1:00 PM. Train tickets not included. Provide arrival train number 2 days before tour. Alternative: Gyeongju Express Bus Terminal pickup available. Emergency contact: +82-54-XXX-XXXX',
      'departure' => 'Transfer to Gyeongju Station at 3:30 PM on Day 4 for 4:00 PM or later KTX train departure. Recommend booking 5:00 PM or 6:00 PM train for buffer time. Alternative drop-off at Express Bus Terminal for bus to Seoul/Busan. Luggage storage available at station. Private taxi to Busan/Ulsan can be arranged (additional cost).',
      'tnc' => 'BOOKING & PAYMENT: Minimum 4 people required (private tour available for 2-3 with 40% surcharge). 30% deposit at booking, full payment 10 days before departure. CANCELLATION: 10+ days: 70% refund. 5-9 days: 50% refund. 2-4 days: 20% refund. Less than 2 days: No refund. ACCOMMODATION: Traditional hanok stay with shared bathroom facilities (ondol floor sleeping on futon). Modern hotel upgrade available (+₩400,000 per person). PHYSICAL REQUIREMENTS: Moderate walking required. Comfortable shoes essential. Temple visits have stairs. Not wheelchair accessible. DRESS CODE: Modest clothing for temples (shoulders/knees covered). Hanbok rental available for photos (₩15,000). WEATHER: Spring (April-May) cherry blossoms and autumn (October-November) foliage are peak seasons - book early. Winter can be cold. SPECIAL: Historian guide provides in-depth historical context - bring curiosity! Photography allowed at most sites (flash prohibited in museums). MEALS: Traditional Korean meals - vegetarian options available with advance notice.',
      'include' => '3 nights traditional hanok accommodation in Gyeongju (twin/family room sharing, ondol floor sleeping). Daily breakfast (Korean-style with rice, soup, side dishes). All meals included: 3 lunches, 3 dinners (Day 1 welcome dinner, Day 3 farewell dinner, plus Day 2 dinner). Round-trip transfers between Gyeongju Station and accommodation. Professional English-speaking historian tour guide all 4 days. Transportation: comfortable air-conditioned vehicle throughout tour. UNESCO site entrance fees: Bulguksa Temple, Seokguram Grotto, Daereungwon Tomb Complex, Yangdong Folk Village. Museum entries: Gyeongju National Museum, Cheonmachong Tomb interior. Donggung Palace & Wolji Pond entry including night view. Girimsa Temple entrance. Traditional tea ceremony experience at Yangdong Village. Gyeongju guidebook and historical context materials. Bottled water during tours.',
      'exclude' => 'KTX train tickets to/from Gyeongju (Seoul-Gyeongju ₩60,000-80,000 roundtrip, Busan-Gyeongju ₩20,000 roundtrip - book via www.letskorail.com). Travel and medical insurance. Personal expenses, shopping, souvenirs. Optional activities: Bicycle rental ₩15,000/day, hanbok rental for photos ₩15,000, additional temple visits, cooking class ₩80,000, traditional paper-making workshop. Modern hotel upgrade ₩400,000 per person. Private tour supplement for 2-3 people (40% additional). Tips for guide and driver (suggest ₩40,000 per person total). Single room supplement ₩600,000 total. Late-night snacks or drinks. Laundry service. Any items not mentioned in inclusions.',
      'nearby_hotel' => 'Gyeongju Hilton (5-star with golf course and spa), Commodore Hotel Gyeongju (lakeside resort with theme park nearby), Kolon Hotel Gyeongju (business hotel central location), Gyeongju GGU Hotel (modern boutique), Lahan Select Gyeongju (mid-range with traditional elements), Gyeongju Hyundai Hotel (family-friendly near attractions), Benikea Gyeongju Chosun (budget-friendly), Traditional Hanok Guesthouses in Gyeongju Gyochon Village',
      'map_url' => 'https://www.google.com/maps/place/Gyeongju,+South+Korea/@35.8562,129.2247,12z',
    ]);

