    DestinationDetail::create([
      'destination_id' => $incheon->id,
      'itinerary' => json_encode([
        'Day 1 - Historic Port & Chinatown Culture' => 'Meet at Incheon International Airport at 10:00 AM (perfect for layover travelers or red-eye arrivals). Transfer to downtown Incheon (40 minutes via airport railroad). Check-in at 4-star hotel near Chinatown. Begin exploration at Incheon Chinatown, Korea\'s only official Chinatown established in 1884 when Incheon opened as an international port. Walk streets lined with colorful Chinese-style gates (paifang), red lanterns, and unique architecture blending Chinese and Korean influences. Visit Jjajangmyeon Museum dedicated to Korea\'s beloved Chinese-Korean black bean noodle dish invented here in 1905. Lunch at famous jjajangmyeon restaurant - taste the legendary dish where it originated! Explore Fairytale Village with whimsical murals and sculptures. Walk to adjacent Jayu Park (Freedom Park), Korea\'s first Western-style park established 1888, located on hilltop with panoramic views of Incheon Port and Yellow Sea. See the statue of General MacArthur commemorating Incheon Landing during Korean War. Visit nearby Open Port Area to see preserved buildings from Japanese colonial period, old banks, and warehouses converted to cultural spaces. Evening at Sinpo International Market, bustling traditional market famous for dakgangjeong (sweet crispy fried chicken) invented here - sample from multiple stalls! Try various Korean street foods and buy souvenirs. Welcome dinner at Chinese-Korean restaurant featuring tangsuyuk (sweet and sour pork). Return to hotel.',
        
        'Day 2 - Island Beaches & Natural Wonders' => 'Morning departure (9:00 AM) to Yeongjong Island where the airport is located. Visit Eurwangni Beach, a beautiful 700-meter sandy beach facing west toward China across Yellow Sea. Depending on tide schedule, witness or learn about impressive tidal flats (up to 2km of exposed seabed during low tide) - one of world\'s most dramatic tidal ranges. Walk along beach promenade, breathe fresh sea air, collect shells. Visit nearby cafes for ocean views. Drive to Wangsan Beach and Yongyudo Island (connected by bridge) for more coastal scenery and fresh seafood. Lunch at seafood restaurant featuring grilled fish, seafood pancakes, and clam soup. Afternoon visit to Incheon Grand Park, massive 727-hectare park with botanical gardens, lakes, forests, and walking trails. Option to visit Incheon Children\'s Museum or Zoo if traveling with kids. Take cable car to mountain peak for city views. Alternatively visit Muui-do Island (ferry required, weather dependent) for quiet beach experience and cycling. Return to Incheon city center. Evening free time for shopping at Bupyeong Underground Shopping Mall or Lotte Department Store. Dinner on own - guide provides recommendations for Korean BBQ or hotpot.',
        
        'Day 3 - Future City & Departure' => 'Morning visit to Songdo International Business District, Korea\'s futuristic smart city built on reclaimed land featuring eco-friendly skyscrapers, sensor-based systems, and visionary urban planning. Walk through Songdo Central Park, inspired by New York\'s Central Park, featuring Korea\'s first seawater canal where you can take water taxi rides. See Tri-Bowl performing arts center with its distinctive three dome architecture. Visit NCube Canal Walk with modern shops and cafes along waterways. Photo opportunities at futuristic buildings and art installations. Experience what Korean cities of the future might look like! Option to visit nearby Compact Smart City Exhibition if interested in urban planning and technology. Browse Hyundai Premium Outlet Songdo for last-minute shopping at discount designer brands. Late check-out at 12:00 PM. Lunch at Songdo or airport. Transfer to Incheon International Airport for 6:00 PM check-in. If you have time before flight, explore the airport\'s many attractions: Korean Cultural Street, Traditional Performance Hall, free showers, relaxation areas, Gardens, Museums. Perfect end to your Incheon adventure!',
