      'destination_id' => $daegu->id,
      'itinerary' => json_encode([
        'Day 1 - Markets & Street Culture' => 'Arrive at Daegu Station (KTX high-speed train from Seoul 2 hours or Busan 40 minutes) at 2:00 PM. Guide welcomes and transfers to 4-star hotel in Dongseongno area, Daegu\'s main shopping and entertainment district (15-minute drive). Check-in and freshen up. Begin city exploration at massive Seomun Market, one of Korea\'s oldest and largest traditional markets operating for over 400 years with 4,000+ shops. Navigate the maze of alleyways selling textiles, Korean fabrics, clothing, dried seafood, traditional medicine ingredients, accessories, and street food. Try local specialties: napjak mandu (flat dumplings), tteokbokki (spicy rice cakes), and various Korean snacks. Experience authentic Korean market culture - energetic, colorful, and delicious! Continue to Kim Gwangseok Street, nostalgic alley dedicated to beloved Korean folk singer who was born in Daegu. See murals depicting his life, bronze statues, and small museum. Live street performances often occur here. Evening exploration of Dongseongno Shopping District, bustling pedestrian street filled with fashion stores, cosmetic shops, trendy cafes, restaurants, and entertainment venues. Popular with young Koreans - feel the energetic youth culture. Welcome dinner at famous Daegu makchang (grilled intestines) restaurant - local specialty not for faint-hearted but delicious! Or choose Korean BBQ option. Return to hotel, evening free for cafe hopping or nightlife.',
        
        'Day 2 - Heritage & Mountain Views' => 'Morning visit (9:00 AM) to Yangnyeongsi Oriental Medicine Cultural Center and Museum, unique attraction showcasing Daegu\'s 350-year history as Korea\'s center for traditional medicine. Learn about Korean herbal medicine (hanyak), see medicinal herbs, understand diagnosis methods, try foot baths with herbal water, and get free health consultation based on traditional Eastern medicine principles. Walk through Yangnyeongsi Medicine Alley where dozens of shops sell ginseng, dried herbs, and traditional remedies. Continue to nearby Daegu Modern History Streets, preserved colonial-era buildings, former missionary houses, churches, and museums telling stories of Korea\'s modernization period and Daegu\'s role in independence movement. Visit Gyesan Catholic Cathedral built 1902. Lunch at traditional Korean restaurant in Jungangno area. Afternoon drive (30 minutes) to Apsan Park, mountain park surrounding Daegu offering spectacular city views. Take cable car to observatory at 500 meters elevation for 360-degree panorama of entire Daegu metropolitan basin surrounded by mountains - stunning vista! Option to hike trails or visit nearby Gatbawi Buddha statue. Gatbawi is famous 9th-century stone Buddha on Palgongsan Mountain (40-minute drive) - legend says Buddha grants one sincere wish, popular with students praying for exam success. Return to city. Dinner on own with guide\'s recommendations.',
        
        'Day 3 - Theme Parks & Tower Views' => 'Fun-filled day starting with visit to Duryu Park (10:00 AM), Daegu\'s largest urban park featuring gardens, walking trails, and Woobang Tower Land (older amusement park). Main attraction: E-World Theme Park, modern amusement park with exciting rides, beautiful gardens, seasonal festivals, and iconic 83 Tower. Spend afternoon enjoying roller coasters, drop towers, music shows, and exploring themed areas. Park is especially beautiful during spring with cherry blossoms or autumn with fall colors. Lunch at park restaurants (various options available). Continue fun at E-World until evening. As darkness falls, ascend the 83 Tower (202 meters tall, named for 1983 completion year), Daegu\'s landmark observation tower offering spectacular night panorama of Daegu cityscape with millions of lights. Enjoy Sky Lounge cafe at tower. Walk around illuminated E-World at night - romantic and magical with colorful lights and fountains. Special farewell dinner at downtown Daegu featuring chimaek (Korean fried chicken and beer) - Daegu specialty! Or choose upscale Korean restaurant. Evening option: explore Daegu\'s famous nightlife in Suseong Lake area (romantic lakeside with cafes and duck-boat rides) or Rodeo Street (youthful club and bar district).',
        
        'Day 4 - Cultural Exploration & Departure' => 'Free morning based on departure schedule and personal interests. Recommendations for optional activities: Visit National Debt Repayment Movement Memorial Hall learning about Daegu citizens\' heroic effort in 1907 to save Korea. Explore Daegu Art Museum with contemporary Korean art. Walk through Gyeongsan Yeongnam University campus area (trendy student district). Shop at Dongdaegu Complex shopping mall. Visit Bangcheon Market for agricultural products and food. Relax at Korean spa (jjimjilbang) for massage and sauna. Browse boutique cafes in Suseong-gu district. Buy local souvenirs: Daegu apples (in season), traditional fabrics, oriental medicine products. Check-out at 12:00 PM. Quick lunch at famous Dongin-dong jjimdak (braised chicken) alley - Daegu food specialty! Transfer to Daegu Station for 5:00 PM or later departure via KTX train to Seoul/Busan. Alternative: Continue to nearby Gyeongju (1-hour drive) for extended trip. Safe journey home with authentic Korean urban experience!',
      ]),
      'arrival' => 'Pick-up at Daegu Station (KTX terminal, connected to East Daegu Station) at 2:00 PM on Day 1. Guide will wait at main exit with "ACP Tours - Daegu" sign. Please book KTX train from Seoul Station (depart 11:30 AM, 2 hours, ₩50,000) or Busan Station (depart 1:00 PM, 40 minutes, ₩15,000). Train tickets not included. Provide train details 2 days before tour. Alternative meeting: Dongdaegu Station or Daegu Airport. Contact: +82-53-XXX-XXXX',
      'departure' => 'Check-out 12:00 PM on Day 4. Transfer to Daegu Station for 5:00 PM or later KTX departure. Recommend booking 6:00 PM or 7:00 PM train for comfortable timing. Seoul-bound trains depart every 30 minutes. Bus to Seoul also available from Express Bus Terminal (4 hours, ₩25,000). Luggage storage at station if needed.',
      'tnc' => 'BOOKING: Minimum 2 people required. Suitable for all ages and fitness levels. PAYMENT: 30% deposit at booking, full payment 7 days before departure. CANCELLATION: 7+ days: 75% refund. 3-6 days: 50% refund. Less than 3 days: No refund. THEME PARK: E-World entrance fee NOT included (₩40,000-55,000 depending on season, includes 83 Tower). Purchase at gate or pre-book for discount. Park closed on some weekdays in winter. WEATHER: Most activities indoor/outdoor mix - tour operates rain or shine. Summer (June-August) very hot in Daegu (30-35°C), bring sunscreen and hat. FOOD: Daegu specialties can be spicy and adventurous (intestines, chicken feet) - alternative options always available. Vegetarian meals possible with 3-day advance notice. SHOPPING: Seomun Market and Dongseongno offer excellent Korean fashion and cosmetics at lower prices than Seoul. Bargaining possible at traditional markets. PEAK SEASON: Daegu Chimac (Chicken & Beer) Festival in July - book accommodations early if attending.',
      'include' => '3 nights accommodation at 4-star hotel Dongseongno central area (twin sharing, modern rooms). Daily breakfast buffet (Western and Korean options). Round-trip transfers between Daegu Station and hotel. Professional English-speaking tour guide Days 1-4. Transportation: comfortable air-conditioned vehicle throughout tour. Entrance fees: Yangnyeongsi Museum, Apsan cable car, 83 Tower observatory (if E-World not entered). 2 group dinners (Day 1 welcome dinner, Day 3 chimaek farewell dinner). Bottled water during tours. Daegu city map and shopping guidebook. Cashbee transport card with ₩8,000 credit.',
      'exclude' => 'KTX train tickets to/from Daegu (Seoul-Daegu ₩50,000 each way, Busan-Daegu ₩15,000 each way - book at letskorail.com). Travel and medical insurance. Lunch all days (estimate ₩10,000-15,000 per meal). Dinner Day 2 (own arrangement). E-World Theme Park entrance (₩40,000-55,000 includes 83 Tower) OR separate 83 Tower only ticket (₩10,000). Optional activities: Woobang Tower Land ₩20,000, Suseong Lake duck-boat rides ₩15,000, spa/jjimjilbang ₩12,000, additional museums, cooking class. Personal expenses, shopping, souvenirs. Gatbawi Buddha site donation (suggested ₩5,000). Tips for guide and driver (suggest ₩45,000 per person total). Single room supplement ₩700,000 total. Nightclub or bar entrance fees. Any items not in inclusions.',
      'nearby_hotel' => 'Inter-Burgo Exco Daegu (5-star convention hotel), Novotel Ambassador Daegu (4-star international chain), Hotel Susung (boutique with spa), Eldis Regent Hotel (business hotel), Hotel Ariana (modern mid-range), Daegu Grand Hotel (affordable near station), Benikea Jungangno Hotel (budget-friendly central), Goodstay Hotel (economy option)',
      'map_url' => 'https://www.google.com/maps/place/Daegu,+South+Korea/@35.8714,128.6014,11z',
    ]);

